# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: The player separates their own cards into two piles, and the opponent chooses one.
# Forcing: Death or Glory is the only spell in hand and five Plains pay for it.
# AI behavior: The AI chooses which pile is exiled; the other pile returns to the battlefield.
# Failure modes:
#   PASS = the player splits the three graveyard creatures, one pile is exiled and the other returns.
#   FAIL = no pile request reaches the player, or the piles do not match the submitted split.
# Card roles:
#   Death or Glory — the self-separated pile effect under test.
#   Grizzly Bears, Savannah Lions, Hill Giant — the creature cards to separate.
[metadata]
Name:Death or Glory (self separation)
Goal:Win
Turns:4
Difficulty:Tutorial
Description:Cast Death or Glory and separate the creature cards in your graveyard into two piles.

